result.summary:
I added lib.SafeRegisterEvent, lib.SafeRegisterUnitEvent and lib.SafeRegisterEvents to /mnt/d/Profile/Users/Tushar/Documents/GIT/LibKa0s/LibKa0s/Core.lua. Core stays at minor 8, because LK-10 already bumped it and v1.56.0 has not shipped.

How they work:
- If C_EventUtils.IsEventValid exists and answers false, the name is rejected and never passed to RegisterEvent.
- Otherwise the call runs as pcall(target.RegisterEvent, target, event, ...). This works for AceEvent objects, Frames and Bus targets, and a Bus target still records the registration so it can replay it.
- `rejected` is an optional array the caller owns. A refused name is added once, never twice. The library keeps no state and prints nothing.
- Every new function is CCN 8 or below.

Tests: I wrote seven cases in tests/test_core.lua first and saw them fail for the right reason ("attempt to call field 'SafeRegister...' (a nil value)"), then implemented until they passed. Two of the cases run twice, once with C_EventUtils present and once with it set to nil, using the kit's __badEvents and C_EventUtils mocks. The others cover:
- the front gate never calling RegisterEvent;
- a raw frame with no rejected list;
- a Bus stand-down followed by stand-up, which replays the registration.

Docs: docs/api/Core/version-8-docs.md now lists the three members (Since 8), explains the front gate and the pcall fallback, and has a Degradation section with the one-rung stub bodies (pcall, no front gate) that consumer Core stubs need so Kit.assertSurfaceParity stays green. Other ripples:
- members-8.json and docs/test-cases.md regenerated (1548 cases);
- a CHANGELOG entry under v1.56.0, and I corrected the LK-10 bullet that said minor 8 adds no member;
- README's one-line Core description updated;
- C_EventUtils added to .luacheckrc as a read global.

Resolves the library half of AuraMaster-R-05.

